<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="Understand what GuideHollow stores locally, how browser tools and search work, and what GitHub Pages and external links may collect." breadcrumbs={[{name:'Privacy Policy',url:'/privacy-policy/'}]}>
<header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow mint">/ privacy_policy</p><h1>Your inputs<br />stay with you.</h1><p>Effective October 23, 2026. This notice describes the site's current configuration.</p></header><article class="prose info-content"><h2>Who operates this site</h2><p>GuideHollow is maintained by emfls through the <a href="https://github.com/emfls/guidehollow">GuideHollow GitHub project</a>. Our available contact channel is described on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. The issue tracker is public; do not post sensitive details.</p><h2>Browser tools</h2><p>The AI Prompt Builder combines text locally in your browser. The response checklist tracks checkmarks locally in the open page. We do not send these inputs to an AI service, backend, database, or analytics endpoint. Inputs and checkmarks are not intentionally saved between page loads. Your browser or extensions may independently provide form restoration.</p><p>Copying writes the selected output to your device clipboard when permitted. Downloading creates a text file on your device. Other apps or users of the device may be able to access these items.</p><h2>Search</h2><p>Search downloads a static index from this website and filters it in your browser. Search terms appear in the page URL. A search URL you open or share may be visible in browser history, hosting logs, and to someone who receives that link. Avoid entering confidential information in search.</p><h2>Local storage and cookies</h2><p>The site uses one localStorage entry, <code>gh-theme</code>, to remember an explicitly selected light or dark theme. Without that preference, it follows your system appearance. You can remove this setting through your browser's site storage controls. The site works if storage is unavailable.</p><p>GuideHollow does not currently set advertising or analytics cookies, load third-party fonts, run analytics, or display ads. We do not run user accounts, a mailing list, comments, or a contact form on this site.</p><h2>Hosting and external services</h2><p>GitHub Pages serves the website and may process technical information such as IP addresses and request details for security and operation. GitHub controls its own handling and retention of that data; see the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.</p><p>Links to GitHub and other external sites take you to services with their own policies. Submitting a public issue to GitHub sends the content and associated account information to GitHub. We do not control those services.</p><h2>Future advertising</h2><p>AdSense verification and advertising support are present in the source code but disabled at launch. If advertising is introduced, we will update this notice and implement the applicable consent choices before enabling ad requests. An AdSense Publisher ID alone does not enable ad serving in this site.</p><h2>Your choices and questions</h2><p>You can browse without submitting information, disable JavaScript, remove local storage, and avoid external links. JavaScript is needed for interactive search, theme switching, copy buttons, and automatic tool behavior.</p><p>Use the public contact route for a general privacy question without including personal details. A private contact channel and fuller operator information are still required before accepting confidential requests. We will revise this notice when site features or data practices change.</p></article>
</Base>
